
4) After first login — this is a KIAUH image
--------------------------------------------
KIAUH and the usual component git trees / venvs are already on the card
under /opt/fly-kiauh and are copied into your home on the first boot that
has a real user. Bind also seeds moonraker.conf, a printer.cfg stub, and
nginx sites for Fluidd (:80) and Mainsail (:4409).

Do not install Simple-AF (pellcorp) on this card.
Ignore any Simple-AF INSTALL_CMD / boot-display / GrumpyScreen / AUTO_CAMERAS
notes above — this image's fly-start.txt is Wi-Fi and accounts only.

SSH in as the user you created, then:

  fly-kiauh
  # menu: Start KIAUH / Add USB cameras
  # same as:  ~/kiauh/kiauh.sh
  # cameras:  fly-kiauh cameras
  #        or fly-crowsnest-add-cams

Edit ~/printer_data/config/printer.cfg (MCU serial) before enabling Klipper.
Skip Moonraker "speedups" / uvloop compile on this 512 MB board.

KlipperScreen is optional and fragile on 512 MB (dpkg can segfault). If you
install it and apt breaks:

  sudo dpkg --configure -a
  fly-klipperscreen-prep    # then retry in KIAUH (X11)

KIAUH community extensions — heavy on 512 MB (prefer phone/PC companions):
  AVOID:  OctoEverywhere, OctoApp, Obico, OctoPrint, Spoolman (Docker),
          DroidKlipp (needs KlipperScreen)
  CAUTION: Mobileraker, Telegram Bot, Moongate (at most one)
  OK:     SimplyPrint, KAMP, TMC Autotune, gcode_shell_cmd, themes,
          PrettyGCode, Klipper-Backup

Do NOT install OctoEverywhere on-device — use the companion app.
Full list: docs/kiauh-fly-lite.md in the fly-debian repo.

USB cameras (after Crowsnest exists):

  fly-kiauh cameras
  # or:  fly-crowsnest-add-cams
